From 356f836feab755c45b2af5b12da1c2b834e928b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vernon Mauery <vernon.mauery@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:30:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] rakp: prevent RAKP1 relabeling of active sessions

RAKP Message 1 derives a session's identity and privilege but was
accepted regardless of session state or packet source. An attacker who
knew a session's BMC session ID could send a second RAKP1 to relabel an
already-authenticated session, and the previously installed integrity/
confidentiality packet keys were retained across the change.

 - Reject RAKP1 unless the session is in setupInProgress, so an active
   session's identity and privilege can no longer be altered.
 - Bind the originating requester tuple (source IP + port) at Open
   Session and verify RAKP1 arrives from the same endpoint.
 - Invalidate derived integrity/confidentiality state and the session
   integrity key on re-derivation so no stale packet keys survive.
 - Add regression tests covering the state and requester-tuple guards.

Tested: added 4 unit test cases for RAKP1
        After applying fix, relabeling a session fails

Upstream-Status: Backport [Security, https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-net-ipmid/+/97460]
Fixes: CVE-2026-16140
Change-Id: I0d7b3d6aff2599a9416bcdd1b81ef2f8bbd48d37
Signed-off-by: Vernon Mauery <vernon.mauery@gmail.com>
Reported-by: HD Moore
Reported-by: Gadi Evron
